Initial scaffold: Launcher + Queens (playable)

Static-site reimplementation of LinkedIn-style puzzle games, modeled
after the Fragrance web project: zero build, vanilla HTML/CSS/JS,
deployable straight to GitHub Pages.

- Launcher (index.html): four game cards with LinkedIn-light theme;
  Queens is playable, the rest are Coming Soon placeholders.
- Queens (games/queens.html): SVG board, region coloring, cycle
  empty -> mark -> queen on click, live violation detection (row,
  column, 8-neighborhood, color region), reveal-solution overlay,
  timer, localStorage prefs and solve log.
- Shared CSS tokens (css/common.css, css/game.css) and JS utilities
  (js/common.js: storage, timer, mulberry32 RNG, helpers).
- Queens uses a deliberately naive in-browser dummy generator
  (randomized backtracking for queen placement + balanced random
  flood fill for color regions). The "real" generation algorithm
  will be designed from scratch later -- the existing BackUp repo's
  generator was intentionally not consulted.
